    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4226" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atarnĕa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτάρνα</span>, Steph. Byz.;
		more com. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀταρνεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Mysia</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 30, 32, § 122</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atarnĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Atarnea</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 56, § 156</span></i>; cf. Mann. Asia Min. III. pp. 398
			and 415.</div>
